esult": {"text": "42", "elapsed_s": 0.6094493769924156, "ttft_s": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 3, "prompt_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 50, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 47, "prompt_ms": 460.136, "prompt_per_token_ms": 9.790127659574468, "prompt_per_second": 102.14371403237303, "predicted_n": 3, "predicted_ms": 50.611000000000004, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.305500000000002, "predicted_per_second": 39.51710102546877}, "finish_reason": "stop", "decode_tps_client": null, "end_to_end_output_tps": 4.922476112461977, "full_output_budget": false}}, {"name": "json", "pass": true, "result": {"text": "{\"ready\": true, \"count\": 3}", "elapsed_s": 1.188450280984398, "ttft_s": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 12, "prompt_tokens": 37, "total_tokens": 49, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 37, "prompt_ms": 437.557, "prompt_per_token_ms": 11.825864864864865, "prompt_per_second": 84.56041155780846, "predicted_n": 12, "predicted_ms": 273.291, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.844636363636365, "predicted_per_second": 40.250136301597934}, "finish_reason": "stop", "decode_tps_client": null, "end_to_end_output_tps": 10.0971830222972, "full_output_budget": false}}, {"name": "extract", "pass": true, "result": {"text": "13", "elapsed_s": 0.5697861749795265, "ttft_s": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 3, "prompt_tokens": 40, "total_tokens": 43, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 40, "prompt_ms": 439.999, "prompt_per_token_ms": 10.999975000000001, "prompt_per_second": 90.90929752113072, "predicted_n": 3, "predicted_ms": 50.54, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.27, "predicted_per_second": 39.57261574990107}, "finish_reason": "stop", "decode_tps_client": null, "end_to_end_output_tps": 5.265133012586336, "full_output_budget": false}}]}, "bench": {"tier": "development", "anchor": null, "warmup": {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one disk to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be verified, restored quickly, and protected from the very threats it is meant to defend against.\n\nHere is a detailed guide on designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nA hybrid approach is usually the most efficient. You should not rely on a single method, but rather a schedule that balances storage space with recovery speed.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies every selected file and folder", "elapsed_s": 4.000164726981893, "ttft_s": 0.8505829239729792, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 182, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 54, "prompt_ms": 470.84700000000004, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.71938888888889, "prompt_per_second": 114.68693652078062, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3149.59, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.79992125984252, "predicted_per_second": 40.32270867001736}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.32281361248408, "end_to_end_output_tps": 31.998682238412577, "full_output_budget": true}, "measured": [{"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored. \n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard **3-2-1 Backup Rule**:\n*   **3** copies of your data (the original and two backups).\n*   **2** different media types (e.g., an internal hard drive and an external USB", "elapsed_s": 4.076468934013974, "ttft_s": 0.9334321049973369, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 472.583, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.592418181818182, "prompt_per_second": 116.38167263739913, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3142.949, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.747629921259843, "predicted_per_second": 40.407909896088036}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.40678073751192, "end_to_end_output_tps": 31.399724141639005, "full_output_budget": true}, {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored quickly and accurately during a disaster.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundation: The 3-2-1 Backup Rule\nBefore diving into specific methods, every reliable system should adhere to the **3-2-1 Rule**:\n*   **3** copies of your data (the original and two backups).\n*   **2** different media types (e.g., an", "elapsed_s": 4.075466853973921, "ttft_s": 0.9309063659748062, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 467.85900000000004, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.506527272727274, "prompt_per_second": 117.55678527077602, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3144.384, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.758929133858267, "predicted_per_second": 40.38946897071096}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.38720211765115, "end_to_end_output_tps": 31.40744473855536, "full_output_budget": true}, {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be verified, restored quickly, and protected from the same threats that affect the primary data.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Methodologies: Full vs. Incremental\nTo balance storage efficiency with recovery speed, a hybrid approach is recommended.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies every selected file and folder, regardless of whether they have changed since the last backup.\n*   **", "elapsed_s": 4.1696858769864775, "ttft_s": 1.02641708398005, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 470.265, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.550272727272727, "prompt_per_second": 116.95533369483164, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3143.379, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.751015748031495, "predicted_per_second": 40.40238227716098}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.40379883596557, "end_to_end_output_tps": 30.69775608432844, "full_output_budget": true}], "decode_tps_client_median": 40.40379883596557, "ttft_s_median": 0.9334321049973369, "pass": true, "distinct_output_texts": 3}, "long": {"tier": "development", "anchor": {"text": "BOLT-7319-CEDAR", "elapsed_s": 11.234010141983163, "ttft_s": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 11, "prompt_tokens": 8238, "total_tokens": 8249, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 8238, "prompt_ms": 10869.294, "prompt_per_token_ms": 1.319409322651129, "prompt_per_second": 757.9149114928716, "predicted_n": 11, "predicted_ms": 257.843, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.7843, "predicted_per_second": 38.783290607074846}, "finish_reason": "stop", "decode_tps_client": null, "end_to_end_output_tps": 0.9791694916574241, "full_output_budget": false}, "warmup": {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from simply \"copying files\" to implementing a **data resilience strategy**. The goal is not just to have a copy of your data, but to ensure that you can recover that data quickly and completely regardless